\title{scSimEval: Unified Benchmarking and Accuracy Evaluation for Single-Cell Multiomics Simulation Methods}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A simple and unified evaluation toolkit for benchmarking single-cell and multiomics data simulation methods. Evaluates how realistic simulated data are compared to real biological datasets across three multiomics experimental designs: (i) paired multiomics (simultaneous co-assay from identical cells, e.g. 10x Chromium Multiome, SHARE-seq, SNARE-seq), which unlocks the full Category 6 multiomics integration and cross-modal alignment suite (joint-embedding Batch ASW, Cell-Type ASW, Graph Connectivity, Integration ARI, and Integration NMI); (ii) unpaired multiomics (independent scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq profiled from separate cells of the same tissue), supported through per-modality unimodal evaluation (Categories 1-5, 7, 8) and joint-embedding integration fidelity; and (iii) mosaic multiomics (partial co-measurement where only a subset of cells has both modalities, e.g. DOGMA-seq or mosaic pooling designs), handled by evaluating the paired and unimodal cell fractions across all 8 canonical categories. The toolkit quantifies simulation realism using 56 evaluation measures organized into 8 canonical categories: (1) Distributional Properties: 10 univariate metrics (Wasserstein, KS, MAD, MAE, RMSE, Bhattacharyya, KDE-ISE, Runs statistic, NN mismatch, Inter-dataset silhouette) and 4 bivariate metrics (Fasano-Franceschini 2D KS, 2D EMD, 2D NN mismatch, 2D Inter-dataset silhouette) evaluated across 7 cell-level, 7 feature-level, and 4 bivariate property pairs, (2) Sparsity & Zero-Inflation Dynamics: logistic dropout curve midpoint/slope/R2 (scRNA-seq), quadratic accessibility-sparsity curve RMSE/R2 (scATAC-seq), and posterior excess zero weight discrepancy, (3) Cellular Manifold & Clustering Concordance: MMD, Generative Precision/Recall, Silhouette ASW, Clustering Deviation Index (CDI), Neighborhood Purity, ARI, and NMI (with auxiliary Davies-Bouldin Index), (4) Technical Variation & Batch Mixing Dynamics: Batch Silhouette, PCR R2, CMS, Inverse Simpson Index (ISI), and Cross-Batch F1, (5) Biological Signal & Differential Fidelity: pseudobulk edgeR-QLF null P-value uniformity, accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC across parallel scRNA-seq DE and scATAC-seq DA sub-categories, (6) Multiomics Integration & Alignment: joint-embedding Batch ASW, Cell-Type ASW, Graph Connectivity, Integration ARI, and Integration NMI, (7) Trajectory & Lineage Topology: HVG-filtered dynverse benchmark (Saelens et al., 2019) comprising HIM topology similarity, edge flip similarity, geodesic distance correlation, branch assignment F1, and Random Forest feature importance weighted correlation (wcor_features), (8) Computational Scalability & Efficiency: core-normalized execution runtime (core_seconds) and memory footprint per allocated core (memory_per_core_mib), with automated multi-core scaling and unified memory_mb resource benchmarking. Includes non-linear low-dimensional cell embedding projections (UMAP, t-SNE, PCA) with quantitative cluster separability (Silhouette) and fidelity (ARI) metrics, automated score normalization, leaderboards, and publication visualizations. Interactive GUI exploration is available via the companion \code{scSimEvalGUI} package.
}
